I haven't run your code as I'm currently on a mobile device but the first thing to find out is if your slowness is from slow calculations on the server or from slow rendering in the client. You can use profvis for the former; your code seems pretty simple though. If the problem is slow rendering, like the json is too complex, you might look at using topojson or a similar tool to simplify your polygons (there's an R package to do this but I can't remember which one, I'm pretty sure it's mentioned on the leaflet for R website though).

